                          Iteration
An Iteration is a fixed period during which an Agile Team plans and completes a selected set of work.

Why do we need Iterations?
Imagine your team has 30 pending development stories.
Instead of trying to complete all 30 together, the team selects a manageable number for the next two weeks

Name	        Campaign Development – Iteration 1
Goal	        Complete campaign creation feature
Start Date	  November 10, 2026
End Date	    November 23, 2026
Capacity	    20 points   amount of work
Focus	         75%    percentage of available team time dedicated to planned iteration work.



                   Story 
A Story is a small, individual piece of work or requirement that an Agile Team plans to complete.


Why do we need Stories? Imagine you have one large project with 50 requirements.
If you track everything as one big task, it becomes difficult to understand:
- What work needs to be completed?
- Who is responsible?
- How much effort is required?
- What is completed?
- What is still pending?
Stories break the work into smaller, manageable items.


What information does a Story contain?  A Story can include details such as:
- Story Name
- Description
- Assigned To
- Priority
- Estimated effort (points or hours)
- Status
- Project association


Story                                                Task                                    Issue
